  "question": {
    "text": "A water fountain on the ground sprinkles water all around it. If the speed of water coming out of the fountain is $\\mathrm{v}$, the total area around the fountain that gets wet is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "eRw4M",
      "text": "\n$\\pi \\frac{v^4}{g^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "0jR5Z",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\frac{v^4}{g^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "usKww",
      "text": "\n$\\pi \\frac{v^2}{g^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "1oI0M",
      "text": "\n$\\pi \\frac{v^4}{g}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Max. range $=\\frac{u^2}{\\mathrm{~g}}$ i.e., $\\frac{v^2}{\\mathrm{~g}}$ (radius of circle)\n$$\n\\text { Area occupied }=\\pi\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{v}^2}{\\mathrm{~g}}\\right)^2=\\frac{\\pi \\mathrm{v}^4}{\\mathrm{~g}^2}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
